1. Scope and definitions

"Software" means the original Qprint code, documentation, and other material
distributed with this license, including modifications to that material. It
excludes third-party material identified by a separate license or provenance.
"Licensor" means each copyright holder, solely to the extent of rights that
holder is entitled to license. "You" means the person or entity exercising
rights under this license.

"Noncommercial Use" means use solely for personal learning, personal projects,
teaching, or academic research, without commercial purpose or commercial
advantage, subject to the following boundaries:

(a) An individual may use the Software for private, unpaid, noncommercial work.
    Being an individual does not exempt consulting, paid work, or business use.
(b) Nonprofit educational and research institutions may use the Software for
    ordinary teaching and academic research. Ordinary tuition, academic
    salaries, scholarships, and public or charitable research grants alone do
    not make that use commercial. Selling access to the Software or providing
    commercial services with it is not covered by this exception.
(c) Internal use by or on behalf of a for-profit business requires a separate
    commercial license, including research, evaluation, and employee use,
    whether or not the Software is distributed or directly generates revenue.
(d) Research commissioned by a business, performed on its behalf, or directed
    toward commercial products or services requires a commercial license.
    An unrestricted donation to an independent nonprofit research institution,
    without commercial deliverables or preferential commercialization rights,
    does not by itself make its independent academic research commercial.
(e) Commercial SaaS, hosted services, paid access, advertising-supported or
    business-promotional services, commercial product integration, resale,
    sublicensing for payment, and bundled commercial distribution require a
    commercial license, including when the Software is only one component.
    A private service limited to an institution's eligible teaching or research
    participants is allowed; a public hosted Qprint service or API offered to
    third parties requires a commercial license even if access is free.

