6. Termination

Your rights terminate automatically upon breach. For a first breach, rights
are reinstated if You fully cure it within 30 days after becoming aware of it;
otherwise reinstatement requires written permission from the relevant
Licensor. Termination requires You to stop exercising the terminated rights.
It does not terminate compliant recipients' independent licenses, erase
liability for past breaches, or authorize continuing commercial use. Sections
5, 7, and 8 survive termination.

